 "intent": "Get per-gene read counts for the reverse-stranded (dUTP, Illumina stranded TruSeq: read 1 is antisense to the transcript) RNA-seq library in sample.fastq with STAR, writing gene_counts.tsv with one gene id and one count per line.",
 "silent_error": "STAR --quantMode GeneCounts writes ReadsPerGene.out.tab with three count columns: column 2 unstranded, column 3 counts for read 1 on the gene strand, column 4 counts for read 1 on the opposite strand. For a dUTP library column 4 is the right one. Taking the first count column (2) ignores strand, so reads that overlap two genes on opposite strands are discarded as ambiguous: geneA gets 12 instead of 24 reads and geneB 6 instead of 12. The table looks like a normal count table and nothing warns about it; the columns are described in the STAR manual (--quantMode GeneCounts).",
